WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan aru nda

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.990
<b>Off the Coast 
of Laboratory 8</b>

14
00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:59.970
<b>"Cruel Fate -
Kuma's Decision as a Father"</b>

15
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.220
"Justice"

16
00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.310
I'm here on business.

17
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.810
It's really cold here...

18
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:10.190
It's totally different from Punk Hazard.

19
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.440
I'll recreate the very future of humankind here.

20
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:21.660
I'm having trouble dealing with
the constant flow of new ideas!

21
00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.580
And yet...

22
00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:29.080
...you didn't know
this laboratory inside out.

23
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.260
What brought you here?

24
00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.890
Every conversation here was overheard.

25
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.850
It's not good to 
secretly negotiate with a pirate.

26
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.020
Shut up!

27
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.520
It's that side of you, Borsalino!

28
00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.110
I don't like that side of you!

29
00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.650
Look, I'm sorry...

30
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.160
But this is what I do...

31
00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.660
Is this Borsalino?

32
00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.960
Yes, I arrived.

33
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.670
You are there, aren't you, Vegapunk?

34
00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.710
Yeah...

35
00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:24.090
This may not concern you, Vegapunk...

36
00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.310
...but even if Bartholomew Kuma would make
an excellent base for the clone soldiers,

37
00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.690
he is a notorious pirate
with a bounty of 296 million berries.

38
00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.150
The Marines would lose face...

39
00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.990
...by possessing clone soldiers
based on such a man.

40
00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.950
Saving face isn't important to science!

41
00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.580
If the cloning project succeeds,
many lives will be saved!

42
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.500
Certainly, if your plan succeeds,

43
00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:54.580
we will gain immense power.

44
00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.750
So here are additional conditions.

45
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.550
The first is, Bartholomew Kuma,

46
00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:07.510
you will join the Seven 
Warlords of the Sea as a pirate.

47
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.230
The other day, a rookie named Ace
took down one of the Warlords,

48
00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.310
and we have been
looking for a replacement.

49
00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.820
The world of pirates
is becoming turbulent.

50
00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.780
You would be perfect for a Warlord.

51
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.700
The second is,

52
00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.790
Kuma, you will become
the Marines' human weapon yourself.

53
00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.040
What?!

54
00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.000
You mean, I must get my body modified?

55
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.330
That is correct.

56
00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:40.340
As a Warlord, that unique power will pose
a significant threat to pirates.

57
00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.300
That would help the Marines a lot.

58
00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.510
Shut up, Kizaru!

59
00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.390
Certainly.

60
00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:51.180
But Kuma also has a prior record
 of Revolutionary activity.

61
00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.850
We do not want him to use that power
against the World Government.

62
00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.610
So the third condition...

63
00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.280
...is that you must ultimately abandon
your mind and free will.

64
00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.870
Wait!

65
00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.370
That's a death sentence, St. Saturn!

66
00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.370
Is this because the other Warlords
won't do what you want?!

67
00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:19.000
A cyborg without free will
is a soulless robot!

68
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.960
Are you telling me to become a murderer?!

69
00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.260
You are in no position to argue with me.

70
00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.300
You are the Marines' scientist.

71
00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:35.230
Those are the three conditions
for saving the life of a criminal's daughter.

72
00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.770
If you cannot accept them,
we have no obligation...

73
00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:43.570
...to spend a fortune on surgeries
to save some nameless girl.

74
00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.200
It's dangerous for you to run in here!

75
00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.330
This is...

76
00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.000
...murder...

77
00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.960
It's inhumane to perform
such a modification surgery...

78
00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.720
Vegapunk.

79
00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.810
I want you to do it.

80
00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.100
Kuma...

81
00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:22.060
I thought he'd make impossible demands
and I wouldn't be able to save Bonney!

82
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.110
I was on pins and needles!

83
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.410
Thank you.

84
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.320
If Bonney gets well,

85
00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:35.080
I will gladly accept any fate!

86
00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.330
Kuma!

87
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.800
Sentomaru-san,
about the matter we discussed...

88
00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:48.840
- Yeah.
- Heave-ho!

89
00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.140
Hey!

90
00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.600
Get back here!

91
00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.810
Vegapunk...

92
00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.940
How long will it take for Kuma's modification
and his daughter's full treatment?

93
00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.490
Sapphire Scales surgeries
will take six months,

94
00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.610
and she'll have to wait
another year before she goes outside.

95
00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.030
So a year and a half in total.

96
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.830
It'll take at least two years
for Kuma's modification.

97
00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.910
I'm so glad...

98
00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.870
Bonney will get well
before her tenth birthday!

99
00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:25.630
Your daughter is essentially a hostage.

100
00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:31.130
Once she recovers,
you will no longer need to obey us.

101
00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.050
I won't run!

102
00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:34.930
Just to be safe,

103
00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:39.220
the World Government
will take custody of her after her surgeries.

104
00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:43.230
Once you lose your free will,
she will be granted freedom.

105
00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.520
Then, Kuma won't get to see her
again after she gets well!

106
00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.480
I guess not.

107
00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.650
Moving forward,
Kuma will undergo modification surgeries...

108
00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.240
...while ruling the seas
as a pirate from the Seven Warlords.

109
00:07:55.700 --> 00:08:00.000
Once her surgeries are complete,
he will be forbidden to contact her or escape.

110
00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.620
If you violate that rule,

111
00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.580
your daughter will be enslaved.

112
00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.250
I will never see her!

113
00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.210
But I just have one request!

114
00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.470
I don't want her to know
the truth about her disease

115
00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.890
or the fact that she is a hostage!

116
00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:20.140
So after her surgeries, instead of making 
her stay at some drab government facility,

117
00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:24.600
I want you to let her rest at the church
in the Sorbet Kingdom where she grew up!

118
00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.560
If you do that,

119
00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.690
I promise I'll never go there to see her

120
00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.400
and I'll do exactly as you command!

121
00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.570
Very well.

122
00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.080
As long as she is under watch,
it doesn't matter where.

123
00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.000
These next two years
are going to be interesting.

124
00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.630
Clank.

125
00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.720
Dad!

126
00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.470
Bonney!

127
00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.810
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

128
00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.560
- Were you a good girl?
- Yeah!

129
00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.480
Uncle!

130
00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:20.950
Bonney, we're going to stay here
for the next six months.

131
00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.540
What?! You're going to be here, too?!

132
00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:28.000
Yeah, I've also found out I have an illness,
so I'm getting tested.

133
00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.500
You too?! Yay!

134
00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.970
This guy's Sentomaru!

135
00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.430
"This guy"?

136
00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.890
She is a handful,
but please look after her.

137
00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.230
Fine...

138
00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.560
Thank you.

139
00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.020
Dad!

140
00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.020
There are so many rooms
without windows here!

141
00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:54.570
Yeah... No, but there are
dangerous things too, so...

142
00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:58.030
Oh, it's fine! You're too much of a chicken!

143
00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.910
Oh hey, Bonney!

144
00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:02.080
Darn... Darn... Darn!

145
00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.580
I'll create the weapons of my dreams!

146
00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.500
Ideas keep flowing!

147
00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.670
Somebody, help write out what's in my brain!

148
00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.250
Eat for me! Go to the bathroom for me!

149
00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.880
I'm too busy! I want to rage!

150
00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.720
Oh, I got another idea!

151
00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.720
I'd welcome even a cat's help!

152
00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:26.730
If only there were five more of me!

153
00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:55.000
Hey!

154
00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.460
Sentomaru!

155
00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.630
You holding up?

156
00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:02.680
Are you free?! I bet you are!
I can play with you!

157
00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.350
I'm not free!

158
00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.060
Aw, really?

159
00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:10.310
Look, I don't have time to hang out with you
every day...

160
00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.070
J-Just for a little while, okay?

161
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.030
Yay!

162
00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:21.530
Oh, hey...

163
00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.230
Oh, Dad!

164
00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:53.810
Bonney!

165
00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.650
Your daughter...

166
00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.860
...lacks any sense of modesty.

167
00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.610
Isn't it nice? He's my horsey!

168
00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.070
Yeah, it is nice, Bonney!

169
00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.080
B-Bonney...

170
00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.290
Don't ask too much of him...

171
00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.330
Okay!

172
00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.790
I don't think she gets it...

173
00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.300
Dad!

174
00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.590
What is it, Bonney?

175
00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.880
H-How did you get so stained?!

176
00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.300
Ta-dah!

177
00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.060
"Dad"

178
00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.060
This is for you!

179
00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:35.020
Thank you! I'll treasure it!

180
00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.480
"Dad"

181
00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:53.960
Oh, that's a VIP seat, Bonney!

182
00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.300
All right, Bonney-chan. See you tomorrow.

183
00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:09.640
Okay...

184
00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.020
I'm hungry...

185
00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.150
This smell must be...

186
00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:28.280
Oh, Bonney!
I was just about to come get you.

187
00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.620
Let's eat it together!

188
00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.290
Pizza!

189
00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:42.630
So good!

190
00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.340
Cheers!

191
00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.300
Hey, Dad! Let's do that thing!

192
00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:51.300
Oh!

193
00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.650
This is the Nika Dance!
Let's dance together!

194
00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.020
Let me try...

195
00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:04.400
Like this?

196
00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:05.650
That's it!

197
00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.530
This is quite hard.

198
00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.120
You're no fun...

199
00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.200
Uncle!

200
00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.540
A-All right...

201
00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.230
<b>Six Months Later</b>

202
00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.690
Great! You're doing well!

203
00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.700
In another year,
you'll be completely cured.

204
00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.120
Thank you, Vegapunk!

205
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.450
Thank you!

206
00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:57.040
Um...

207
00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.160
Once I get well,

208
00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.120
can I come visit?!

209
00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:04.210
Of course!

210
00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:11.800
Dad!

211
00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.510
Is the sea beautiful?

212
00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.970
Yes, it's beautiful.

213
00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.600
I wanna see it...

214
00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:20.940
You'll be able to see it soon.

215
00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.230
Yeah!

216
00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.270
With you!

217
00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.780
Yeah... Can't wait.

218
00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:30.740
<b>Sorbet Kingdom</b>

219
00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.950
Bonney! Kumachi! Welcome home!

220
00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.500
It's been a long time!
You can live here again?

221
00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.000
Yes!

222
00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.380
I'll be cured in a year
and get to go outside!

223
00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:48.170
Oh yeah?! I'm happy for you.

224
00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.840
You said you'd get well before age ten
and you were right!

225
00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:55.260
Does somebody need to be
looked after again?

226
00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.520
<b>Queen Dowager Conney, 
Sorbet Kingdom</b>

227
00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.390
Old Bag Conney!

228
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:03.100
We'll all be happy
to take care of her, Kuma.

229
00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:04.730
Leave her to us!

230
00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.570
Thank you. I'll be relying on you again.

231
00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:11.900
I'm a pirate now,
so I may cause this country trouble...

232
00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:15.490
I probably won't be able to
come back for over a year.

233
00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.910
What?! For that long?!

234
00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:20.160
I'll write you a lot!

235
00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:21.620
Mm-hm! Mm-hm!

236
00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.380
Next time we meet, let's be out on the sea,
watching the horizon together.

237
00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.040
Yeah! Can't wait!

238
00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.170
And I wanna go on many trips!

239
00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:33.380
Yeah! I would love to
take you anywhere you like!

240
00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.140
I would've loved to do it...

241
00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:41.430
Leave it all to me, Kuma-san.

242
00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:48.650
<b>Alpha, an Intelligence Agent 
Cipher Pol No.8</b>

243
00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:43.640
Who is this woman?!

244
00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.310
By the doctor's orders,

245
00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:48.650
I'll stay with Bonney-chan
until she's fully cured.

246
00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.690
Every day, I'll check her temperature,
administer medicine,

247
00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:55.780
and monitor for even the slightest changes!
I'm Alpha, a nurse!

248
00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.120
Nice to meet you, Bonney-chan.

249
00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.630
Hey! What did you build out in front?!

250
00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.790
That's our temporary housing!

251
00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.130
Until she's fully cured,
we can't let anyone suspicious see her,

252
00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.590
so always carry your ID, everyone.

253
00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.680
So inconvenient!

254
00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.600
A child's neck...

255
00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:26.640
Can be crushed just like that.

256
00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:28.940
I know.

257
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.440
I'll never come back.

258
00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.450
Thank you, Bonney.

259
00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.700
For being born.

260
00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.370
What?!

261
00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.640
Okay, I'm heading out.

262
00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.810
Take care!

263
00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.350
Don't worry about Bonney!

264
00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.210
Despite being called the Tyrant,

265
00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:38.470
Bartholomew Kuma was very obedient to orders, and his joining the Seven Warlords...

266
00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:38.470
"Seven Warlords of the Sea"

267
00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:42.430
...shook up pirates across the world.

268
00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:45.720
Young Master. It says
there's a new member of the Seven Warlords.

269
00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.270
Kuma the Tyrant?

270
00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:55.070
We've got another miscreant on our hands.

271
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.320
Are you interested in the new Warlord?

272
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.780
I don't care who it is.

273
00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.530
Anyway,

274
00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:07.000
have you eliminated the witness
to our Rainmaking Ship?

275
00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.710
Yes, flawlessly.

276
00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.170
He's supposedly as huge as Whitebeard.

277
00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.760
Who's stronger? Me or him?

278
00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:20.010
Koby.

279
00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.350
O-Of course, it's you, Alvida-sama!

280
00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.520
Jinbe! They found a replacement!

281
00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:31.980
I'm happy for you.

282
00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:35.020
Who are you to say that, Ace?

283
00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:41.990
There would be no fuss
if you didn't defeat Hanafuda in the first place.

284
00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:45.200
Do you think this new face
will meet your approval?

285
00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.620
I'm trying to see that now.

286
00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.410
A former king?!

287
00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:54.670
Well, there is an active king
in the group as well.

288
00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.800
The world of pirates has changed...

289
00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:00.630
It does not matter to me.

290
00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:04.010
Because I will never go to the central!

291
00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.390
Even so, you still need to know these things,
Snake Princess!

292
00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.970
Hey!

293
00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:13.270
It says he's a Paw Pad Human!

294
00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.560
What kind of power is that?!

295
00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.520
But Moria-sama, he's a Warlord!

296
00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.570
The Seven Warlords work
directly under the Government, right?!

297
00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.660
Kuma-san wouldn't join such a group!

298
00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:36.130
"Dear Bonney, I'm writing to you at sea.

299
00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:42.840
"Dad"

300
00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.420
I became a little famous,
so it is difficult to travel now,

301
00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:41.800
but I'm doing okay."

302
00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.300
Sorry, it's far. Thanks.

303
00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.470
"How's everyone?

304
00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.980
I'll try to find many places...

305
00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.980
...that I would like to visit with you
when you turn ten."

306
00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.320
Bartholomew Kuma,
you have a new order from the Government.

307
00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:04.740
Where are you?

308
00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.370
It's mad!

309
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.330
I'm in the East Blue.

310
00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.580
What is the order?

311
00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.980
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

312
00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.770
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

313
00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:44.070
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

314
00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.650
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

315
00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:50.030
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

316
00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:55.540
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

317
00:21:55.540 --> 00:22:01.420
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

318
00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.380
We
bokura wa

319
00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:04.880
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end
EVERYDAY owarenai

320
00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.510
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated
EVERYDAY makerenai

321
00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:11.300
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

322
00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.810
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

323
00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.520
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

324
00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:21.860
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

325
00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.570
Don't be afraid
ojikedukuna yo

326
00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:28.530
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

327
00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.030
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

328
00:22:32.780 --> 00:22:33.620
Now, move aside
saa doite

329
00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:36.250
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

330
00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:38.830
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

331
00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:41.500
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

332
00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.550
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kiduita no
